Given the above it's hard to enumerate all that you should consider.
A few important things... Do you have magic resistance? You need it.
Do you have fire resistance? Necessary for Gehennom. Then, exchange
your body armor for some dragon scale mail (dragons may drop scales
and you wear them and read a scroll of enchant armor). You seem not
to have intrinsic protection; so collect money, 400 times your
experience level, and donate it to some priest (if you are already
in Gehennom the priest at the end of Death Valley might be the one
to be the nearest). Have you already done the quest? Have you been
in the mines and got the luckstone? And avoid these minotauri, they
hit very hard.

